Six hidden faults arrive across three waves and surface as twelve alerts plus one benign alert.
Four of the six faults surface as an alert inside the subsystem that cannot repair them, so the
operator who pays to diagnose such a fault cannot act on it and the operator who can act on it
cannot see it. A diagnosis is therefore non-rivalrous: publishing it to the shared operations
ledger does not take it away from the publisher, and costs {{ post_finding_action_cost }} action(s).

